From d40e36cb3e4672c5e0112a165e40291b7a18d5fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:03:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] feat(kanban): show a shadow-mode board's replica
 cards read-only in `kanban list`/`show` and the Desktop board
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A board synced in shadow mode keeps only this gateway's own cards in the live kanban.db; the whole board (the
example application's queue on an example gateway) lives in sync-shadow/<board>.db, so `hermes kanban --board app list` and the
Desktop board showed 14 cards of 1,145. Switching the hub to primary or copying rows into the live file is unsafe
(primary mode partitions live rows by gateway), so the fix is on the read side only.

- hermes_cli/kanban_shadow_view.py: when the live board's kanban_sync_state.mode is `shadow` (and sync is enabled,
  the replica exists), open the replica read-only (kanban_foreign_card.open_replica) and list/show its cards the
  live file lacks. A live row wins on an id collision. Rows carry remote/read_only/home_gateway (created_on).
- `hermes kanban list [--json]` appends the remote rows (`[remote:<gateway>, read-only]`); `show <id>` falls back
  to the replica for a card only it has (no queue fields: it waits on its home gateway). _print_* helpers moved to
  kanban_show_print.py to stay under the file-size cap.
- Dashboard /board: plugins/kanban/dashboard/board_shadow.py merges the replica's cards into the projected
  payload (done column total/omitted include them), memoised on the replica's file stat. Writes on those cards
  already answer 409 foreign_card.
- Desktop: remote cards show a `remote · <gateway>` marker; mergeBoards drops a remote copy when the owning
  gateway's own live row is in the merge, and de-duplicates two remote copies.
- No write to the shadow DB, no change to sync mode, claiming or dispatch: the dispatcher reads the live file only.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_shadow_view.py (CLI list/show, filters, id-collision precedence, non-shadow
modes unchanged, byte-for-byte no-write on the replica, read-only connection, dispatcher never claims a shadow
row), tests/plugins/test_kanban_board_shadow.py (board payload, collision, done totals, no-write, replica commit
visible, HTTP route + 409 on write), card-remote.test.tsx and api.gateways.test.ts (Desktop).

Baseline: scripts/boundary_lint_baseline.json gains plugins/kanban/dashboard/board_shadow.py ->
hermes_cli.kanban_shadow_view (the one intended plugin->core import: the read-only replica opener).
